```

## Abbreviations

Articles start with `manuscript/main/00c_abbreviations.md`; edit or move it
to the journal's required position, or remove it. Reports do not ship a list,
but support the same feature in any document. Use a heading named
Abbreviations / List of abbreviations, or give it the explicit abbreviation id
(`abbreviations`). Write a term line followed by `:   Long form` (or `~`) for each
entry; blank lines, several definitions and indented continuation paragraphs are
supported. Cells accept ordinary Markdown, values, citations and cross-references.
Unreadable lists stay as written and produce a check warning. Only new example
projects get demo entries; an update that adds the file adds the heading and
guidance only.
Lists sort automatically and render as borderless, unnumbered two-column
tables in Word and preview. They do not count toward table limits or appear
in Figures & Tables or the table editor.

Under `[abbreviations]` in `trazo.toml`, choose `style = "table"`, `"list"`
or `"inline"`, set `sort = false` to retain source order, and use `ignore = []`
for deliberate acronym exceptions. Run `scripts/trazo abbreviations check` for advisory
unused/unlisted and first-use definition warnings. Define each term separately
in the abstract and main text (`long form (TERM)` or the reverse); captions
and tables are excluded from the first-use check. Preview text has long-form
hover help, including conservative `s` and `'s` forms. Headings, links, code,
math, values and the document head are not annotated. Article Submission includes
the warnings and a copy-ready inline Abbreviations field. Updates leave an
existing starter list untouched.
